# BRACE record ownership. Copy these lines into .github/CODEOWNERS and replace
# the team names. Turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection
# for the default branch, so changes to these files can't merge without them.
#
# brace.py check verifies approvals itself (it reads the pull request reviews),
# so CODEOWNERS is a second lock, not the only one. Keep the teams here in line
# with approvals.approvers in .brace/deployment.yaml.

# Risk acceptances and N/A decisions: Governance approves.
/.brace/exceptions/          @your-org/ai-governance
/.brace/na/                  @your-org/ai-governance

# What the agent is, its rating, roles, and who may approve: Governance and the Business owner.
/.brace/deployment.yaml      @your-org/ai-governance @your-org/support-business-owner

# The rest of the record: the agent team keeps it up to date; Governance reviews.
/.brace/record.yaml          @your-org/agent-team @your-org/ai-governance
/.brace/manifest.yaml        @your-org/agent-team @your-org/ai-governance

# The checker itself: changing it changes what counts as GO.
/tools/brace/                @your-org/ai-governance
/.github/workflows/brace-check.yml  @your-org/ai-governance
